    "/api/subscribe": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Two live sources, both taken BEFORE a single journal row is read:\n\n- the storage's committed-sequence signal (spec §2.4: raised after each\n  commit that appended to the journal). A commit that lands while the\n  replay is being read shows up as a pending change, so it cannot fall into\n  the gap between the replay's last read and the live phase.\n- the transient bus, for what is never stored: deltas, turn ends, meta.\n\nDurable events reach the client only by reading the journal after\n`last_seq` — in the replay, and again on every signal change in the live\nphase — so each one is sent once, in sequence order, and de-duplication by\n`seq` is structural rather than left to the client. The bus's `Entry` items\nare therefore not forwarded: the same entry arrives as its durable\n`ThreadEntryAppended` event. Bus items for another thread are dropped.",
        "operationId": "subscribe",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "The thread to watch.",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "thread_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ThreadId"
            }
          },
          {
            "description": "The last durable sequence this client has already applied; 0 replays\nthe thread from its start.",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "after",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "format": "int64",
              "type": "integer"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "text/event-stream": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Server-sent events for one thread (spec §2.10): the durable journal after `after`, then `caught-up`, then live. Each frame's `event:` names its kind and its `data:` is JSON unless stated.\n\n- `durable` — `{seq, kind, operation_id, thread_id, payload}`: one journal event. `operation_id` and `thread_id` are the ids it names, `null` where it names none; `payload` is the event's JSON object. Sent once each, in `seq` order, in the replay and live alike; remember the highest `seq` and resubscribe with it as `after`.\n- `caught-up` — `{seq}`: the last replayed `seq`. The replay is over.\n- `delta` — `{op, text}`: streamed text of a running turn. Transient: never replayed.\n- `turn-end` — `{op, subtype, stop_reason}`: the harness finished a turn. Transient.\n- `meta` — `{op, label}`: any other harness line, by label. Transient.\n- `lagged` — empty: this client fell behind and transient frames were dropped; durable ones were not.\n- `fatal` — data is a message as plain text: the journal could not be read and the stream ends.\n\nThe stream also ends when the daemon stops. Reconnect with the last `seq`."
          }
        },
        "summary": "Spec §2.10: durable replay, then a no-gap handoff to live, then\nde-duplication by durable sequence.",
        "tags": [
          "stream"
        ]
      }
    },
